 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all (the initial call and 4 retries).
+Before each retry, larder waits 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds respectively. If the fifth attempt times out, the error is
+raised to the caller. A successful capture returns immediately.
+
+These pauses spread attempts across the gateway's busy periods instead of sending them back to back. They add up
+to 20 seconds of waiting on the member's confirmation page, in addition to the time spent calling the gateway.
+The decision and sandbox replay are recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
